# UI Module

## Purpose

Game presentation UI via RmlUi. Lives outside graphics so the render backend stays toolkit-agnostic. Scenes own a `UIView`; the shell owns `UISystem` for app-lifetime initialise/shutdown.

## Layout

```
src/core/ui/
  UIValue.h              # Game-facing scalar variant
  UIDataModel.h/.cpp     # Declare/Set over RmlUi data models (pimpl)
  UIView.h/.cpp          # Context + document + composite pass (pimpl)
  UISystem.h/.cpp        # Rml::Initialise/Shutdown, font loading
  FontLoadDelegate.h/.cpp # SceneResourceLoader::Delegate for manifest "fonts"
  UIRenderPass.h/.cpp    # AbstractRenderPass writing the composite image
  UIRenderInterface.h/.cpp  # Rml::RenderInterface over Renderer (internal)
  UISystemInterface.h/.cpp  # Rml::SystemInterface (internal)
  shaders/ui.vert/.frag
```

## Includes

| What | Include |
|---|---|
| Game / scene API | `#include <ui/UISystem.h>`, `#include <ui/UIView.h>`, `#include <ui/UIDataModel.h>` |
| RmlUi | Only inside `src/core/ui/*.cpp` and internal headers |

## Key Classes

| Class | Namespace | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| `UISystem` | `eage::ui` | App-lifetime RmlUi init, shared render/system interfaces, fonts |
| `FontLoadDelegate` | `eage::ui` | Manifest `fonts` section loader; register on `SceneResourceLoader` in the shell |
| `UIView` | `eage::ui` | Scene-lifetime context, document, data model, composite pass |
| `UIDataModel` | `eage::ui` | Backend-agnostic Declare/Set for document bindings |

## Dependencies

```
game (StatusPanel, MainScene)
        |
        v
   eage::ui  (public headers are Rml-free)
        |
        +---> graphics (Renderer, AbstractRenderPass, ManagedImage, bindless)
        |
        +---> RmlUi (static lib, only in ui internals)
```

## Usage

```cpp
// Declare keys BEFORE LoadDocument
auto view = std::make_unique<eage::ui::UIView>( ui_system, "main_hud", 640, 360 );
model.Declare( "kill_count", 0 );
view->BindImage( "gameplay", scene_pass->GetColorTarget() );
view->LoadDocument( "./src/game/ui/rml/hud.rml" );
renderer.AddRenderPass( &view->GetRenderPass() );
```

## DOs

- Keep RmlUi includes out of game-facing headers
- Register the gameplay image as a ShaderRead pass input via BindImage
- Tear down UIView before the gameplay SceneRenderPass (composite samples it)
- Use ASCII-only source (MSVC C4819 on code page 936)

## DON'Ts

- Don't include `<RmlUi/...>` from `game/` or other core modules
- Don't call `Context::Render()` from Prepare - it needs a live command buffer in Execute
- Don't use RCSS features that need layers/filters (box-shadow, filter, mask-image, gradients) until those RenderInterface overrides are implemented
- Don't free BindImage textures in ReleaseTexture - they are scene-owned
